{%- comment -%}
  Nailzify concierge widget.

  INSTALL: Online Store -> Themes -> Edit code -> Snippets -> Add a new snippet
  named `nailzify-concierge`, paste this in, then add ONE line to theme.liquid,
  immediately before </body>:

      {% render 'nailzify-concierge' %}

  ⚠️ BEFORE </body>, NOT IN <head>. The script appends to document.body, and a
  head-injected copy would run before body exists. It handles that case, but
  loading render-blocking JS in the head of someone's storefront is rude
  regardless.

  ⚠️ `defer`, NEVER `async`. Both keep the parser unblocked; only `defer`
  guarantees the script runs after the document is parsed. With `async` the
  execution point is whenever the network happens to finish, which is a race
  that shows up on slow connections and not on yours.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Preconnect saves a DNS + TLS round trip on the first message, which lands
  squarely in the customer's perceived time-to-first-token.
{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://{{ shop.domain }}" crossorigin>

<script
  src="{{ 'nailzify-widget.js' | asset_url }}"
  defer
  {%- comment -%}
    Subresource Integrity is deliberately omitted: `asset_url` is versioned by
    Shopify's CDN and the file is replaced on every deploy, so a pinned hash
    would break the widget on each release. The asset is served from Shopify's
    own CDN over TLS.
  {%- endcomment -%}
></script>
